|---|---|
| `childEnv(ghConfig)` | Deletes `GH_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN`; sets `GH_CONFIG_DIR`, `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT='0'`, and `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=1` with `GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0='credential.helper'` / `GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0=''` |
| `ghConfigDir(outPath)` | New: empty folder beside the run log, created once in `runArm` *before* the first snapshot so it is never read back as a path the turn changed |
| `spawnTurn(...)` / `job` | Threads `ghConfig` to the child env |
| `remoteNames()` + `runTurn` first-prompt block | Non-`--dry-run` run exits `2` with `remote_present` when `git remote` prints any name, before the dirty check and before any spawn |
| Module header + "Worktree guards" divider | WHY updated: network reach removed before the model has it, and why the remote check precedes the dirty check |

### Verify output

```
$ node $R --runtime claude --row-id mns-chat-01 --out $X/remote-check.jsonl
{"ok":false,"code":"remote_present","remotes":["origin"]}
exit=2

$ node $R --dry-run --runtime claude --row-id mns-chat-01 --out $X/dry.jsonl
{"ok":false,"code":"worktree_dirty","paths":[".skilled/.../run-command-behaviour.mjs",".../score-command-transcripts.mjs",".../command-transcript-score.vitest.ts",".../007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/acceptance-criteria.md",... 8 more]}
exit=2

